  "id": "COMPOUND:16166 - PROTEIN:5802",
  "verbalization": "Traxillagenin appears to have a dual mechanism of action targeting Hs746T, a key player in cellular processes that are implicated in disease. The evidence suggests that Traxillagenin acts as a target for multiple pathways, with one direct route through the T-cell surface glycoprotein CD3, which is a known component of the T-cell receptor complex. This pathway leads to the activation of Lup-20(29)-en-3-ol, a compound that in turn targets Hs746T. The second pathway also involves CD3, but it leads to the same downstream target, Hs746T, through a different intermediate, 2-(1a,4-dimethyl-3,3a,4,5,6,7,7a,7b-octahydro-2H-naphtho[1,2-b]oxiren-7-yl)prop-2-enoic acid. The overlapping targets and the consistent involvement of CD3 across these pathways suggest a shared biological function, possibly related to immune regulation or cellular signaling. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Traxillagenin to modulate Hs746T through multiple routes, which may have implications for therapeutic applications. The evidence is supported by a consistent pattern of interaction, though the exact functional significance of the intermediate compounds remains to be fully elucidated.",
